      "description": "Agent memory for the platform: durable lessons an agent carries between sessions, one `\"$schema\": \"folio-memory/v1\"` node each, assembled into `.claude/agent-memory/<agent>/MEMORY.md` by `scripts/agent-memory.ts`, which reads EVERY instance's declared `memory` directory. `context`: read during a process, never written by one; it changes when a person directs an authoring agent. Also holds the `interaction` node (how each person wants to be asked, read at session start) and any `folio-waiver/v1` confirmation waivers, told apart by their `$schema` tag. Moved from the repository root on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-06 (bean `ar1s`): memory belongs to the harness its lesson is about, so lessons about content authoring live in the content harness's own `memory/`.",
